WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.318
mello: localhost coursework skills prototype. Fictional demonstration; no therapy, diagnosis, or human monitoring. Start needs no questionnaire or model response.

00:00:07.318 --> 00:00:10.709
Explicit profile: Brief reminders and saved practice context on. Save confirms persistence. Context is factual cue/status, never an inferred diagnosis; raw history is not sent to the model.

00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:12.690
Override remembered Text only with Animated circle for this practice. This changes the cue, not the remembered choice or fixed rhythm.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:01:18.178
Guided skill: four one-second inhale counts, six exhale counts, six cycles. Text and color carry phase; breathing has no app audio. Pause, End and independent Crisis support remain available.

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:21.109
Completed: actual browser sequence and truthful local save status. This is a behavior/timing check, not evidence of clinical improvement.

00:01:21.109 --> 00:01:31.621
History retains local dates, status, timing, initial/final cue and saved conversations. Completed, Stopped, Interrupted and Not started remain different.

00:01:31.621 --> 00:01:43.638
Prepared reply uses saved Brief reminders plus opted-in current/remembered cue and factual completed practice. The local renderer tailors approved text; the model never receives raw saved history.

00:01:43.638 --> 00:01:52.148
Live local model selects an allowlisted topic only. The displayed answer remains reviewed catalog text. Optional voice has readable text, explicit Play/Stop, and no microphone; this video is silent.

00:01:52.148 --> 00:01:59.156
Independent bundled Crisis support opens outside model decisions. Earlier tests physically stopped the API and confirmed this route still opened in the loaded app. No support service is contacted in this fictional demo.

00:01:59.156 --> 00:02:06.166
Accessibility: higher contrast, larger text, words beside colors, keyboard controls, reduced motion and configurable screen-reader updates. Blind-user and full assistive-technology testing remain untested; no conformance claim.
